{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MmeYk7prRQexb2FB68rip1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast Heart Attack mode girlfriend requests list challenges\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://forceforgood.co.uk/?p=11728\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://forceforgood.co.uk/racing/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast/\"},{\"title\":\"Outrun 2006: Gone, But Not Forgotten\",\"url\":\"https://moegamer.net/2017/08/01/outrun-2006-gone-but-not-forgotten/\"},{\"title\":\"Out Run 2006: Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressreader.com/uk/retro-gamer/20210610/281655373001268\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006\",\"url\":\"https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/OutRun_2006\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://games.kikizo.com/reviews/xbox/outrun2006_coast2coast.asp\"},{\"title\":\"www.cheatcc.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.cheatcc.com/?p=61478\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast is a fun game as long as you take it for what it’s worth . by Mike Chasselwaite\",\"url\":\"https://cheatcc.com/articles/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-review-preview-for-pc-pc/\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://gamesradar.com/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-18/2\"},{\"title\":\"www.gamesradar.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamesradar.com/au/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-18/2/\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast review\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamesradar.com/outrun-2-2\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun: Online Arcade\",\"url\":\"https://www.mobygames.com/game/45915\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamesradar.com/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-15\"},{\"title\":\"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast\",\"url\":\"https://retro-replay.com/db/playstation-2/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast\"},{\"title\":\"www.gamespot.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamespot.com/outrun-online-arcade/user-reviews/2200-501237/\"},{\"title\":\"ps2 reviews 478\",\"url\":\"https://psxextreme.com/archive/ps2-reviews-478/\"}]\n\nThe search turned up several sources on Heart Attack mode and the Coast 2 Coast career mode in OutRun 2006.\n\n**Heart Attack mode:** Your girlfriend calls out short, on-the-fly requests, and you have to meet them while still racing the clock. Examples include drifting, keeping your speed up, and driving through cones. One reviewer also listed \"hit the cars\" and \"avoid the UFOs\" among the requests. Heart Attack, meanwhile, is along similar lines but combines the need to race quickly with the additional challenge of satisfying the various whims of your girlfriend. Heart attack mode is an inspired mission mode, where your character's girlfriend calls out brief missions on the fly, which you then have to satisfy. Some of the missions are downright fun, such as \"hit the cars\" and \"avoid the UFOs.\"\n\n**Coast 2 Coast relationship:** This career mode builds on Heart Attack. The missions for the three \"girlfriend\" characters, meanwhile, are primarily based on the Heart Attack mode, with a few additions to the formula to keep things interesting. Other mission types also appear. Coast 2 Coast mode is the game's \"career\" mode, in which there are many challenges (labeled as \"missions\") to complete, which can include racing rivals for the top position, thrilling the player's passenger by completing their requests to execute certain driving maneuvers, or tests of memory and logic.\n\n**Girlfriend request types and progression:** One review describes the requests as ranging from the usual drifting or passing traffic, to breaking through 'lines' that join two approaching vehicles, hitting funny 'ghosts' whose eyes pop out on impact. Progression is gated by performance. You have to impress your girlfriend by completing her driving requests, and only when you have an A rank or higher on her entire map of challenges do you get to unlock the next girlfriend.\n\nI didn't find a complete, official list of every request, so the sources only give examples. For a full catalogue, a dedicated wiki or FAQ would be the next place to check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"554ca1ef-c358-49cf-9a91-1163ce5dd1fd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:24.675Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast Heart Attack mode girlfriend requests list challenges","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FUoLWvn6Y9H5ecpzPFcYjR","content":[{"title":"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://forceforgood.co.uk/?p=11728"},{"title":"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://forceforgood.co.uk/racing/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast/"},{"title":"Outrun 2006: Gone, But Not Forgotten","url":"https://moegamer.net/2017/08/01/outrun-2006-gone-but-not-forgotten/"},{"title":"Out Run 2006: Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://www.pressreader.com/uk/retro-gamer/20210610/281655373001268"},{"title":"OutRun 2006","url":"https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/OutRun_2006"},{"title":"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://games.kikizo.com/reviews/xbox/outrun2006_coast2coast.asp"},{"title":"www.cheatcc.com","url":"https://www.cheatcc.com/?p=61478"},{"title":"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast is a fun game as long as you take it for what it’s worth . by Mike Chasselwaite","url":"https://cheatcc.com/articles/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-review-preview-for-pc-pc/"},{"title":"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://gamesradar.com/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-18/2"},{"title":"www.gamesradar.com","url":"https://www.gamesradar.com/au/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-18/2/"},{"title":"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast review","url":"https://www.gamesradar.com/outrun-2-2"},{"title":"OutRun: Online Arcade","url":"https://www.mobygames.com/game/45915"},{"title":"OutRun 2006 Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://www.gamesradar.com/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast-15"},{"title":"OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast","url":"https://retro-replay.com/db/playstation-2/outrun-2006-coast-2-coast"},{"title":"www.gamespot.com","url":"https://www.gamespot.com/outrun-online-arcade/user-reviews/2200-501237/"},{"title":"ps2 reviews 478","url":"https://psxextreme.com/archive/ps2-reviews-478/"}]},"The search turned up several sources on Heart Attack mode and the Coast 2 Coast career mode in OutRun 2006.\n\n**Heart Attack mode:** Your girlfriend calls out short, on-the-fly requests, and you have to meet them while still racing the clock. Examples include drifting, keeping your speed up, and driving through cones. One reviewer also listed \"hit the cars\" and \"avoid the UFOs\" among the requests. Heart Attack, meanwhile, is along similar lines but combines the need to race quickly with the additional challenge of satisfying the various whims of your girlfriend. Heart attack mode is an inspired mission mode, where your character's girlfriend calls out brief missions on the fly, which you then have to satisfy. Some of the missions are downright fun, such as \"hit the cars\" and \"avoid the UFOs.\"\n\n**Coast 2 Coast relationship:** This career mode builds on Heart Attack. The missions for the three \"girlfriend\" characters, meanwhile, are primarily based on the Heart Attack mode, with a few additions to the formula to keep things interesting. Other mission types also appear. Coast 2 Coast mode is the game's \"career\" mode, in which there are many challenges (labeled as \"missions\") to complete, which can include racing rivals for the top position, thrilling the player's passenger by completing their requests to execute certain driving maneuvers, or tests of memory and logic.\n\n**Girlfriend request types and progression:** One review describes the requests as ranging from the usual drifting or passing traffic, to breaking through 'lines' that join two approaching vehicles, hitting funny 'ghosts' whose eyes pop out on impact. Progression is gated by performance. You have to impress your girlfriend by completing her driving requests, and only when you have an A rank or higher on her entire map of challenges do you get to unlock the next girlfriend.\n\nI didn't find a complete, official list of every request, so the sources only give examples. For a full catalogue, a dedicated wiki or FAQ would be the next place to check."],"durationSeconds":7.3805367970000075,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MmeYk7prRQexb2FB68rip1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PWpEC59CP7WVmjuCQLPQdc","type":"tool_result","content":"# OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast: Gameplay Summary\n\n**Core driving and cars**\n- Gameplay is similar to earlier *OutRun 2* versions. Cars are grouped into classes from Novice to Professional. Higher classes have greater top speeds and weaker handling.\n- A separate \"OutRun\" class gives each car better performance in all areas, plus cosmetic changes such as racing stripes, decals, and reworked bodywork.\n- The game has 15 cars, the most of any *OutRun* title. Ten come from *OutRun 2 SP*, and new models include the 550 Barchetta, F355 Spider, Superamerica, 328 GTS, and F430.\n\n**Modes**\n- **Coast 2 Coast** is the career mode. Its missions include racing rivals for first place, fulfilling a passenger's requests for specific driving maneuvers, and tests of memory and logic.\n- Returning from *OutRun 2 SP* are the \"OutRun,\" \"Heart Attack,\" and \"Time Attack\" modes.\n- Four modes are exclusive to Coast 2 Coast:\n  - **Test Your Drift:** A one-on-one race where points come from drifting through bends.\n  - **Test Your Slipstream:** Drive behind traffic to collect points and beat rivals.\n  - **Avoid the Knockout:** The last-placed car at the end of each stage is eliminated.\n  - **Don't Lose Your Girlfriend:** A one-on-one duel to stay ahead of a rival couple until their \"heart points\" reach 0.\n\n**Unlocks**\n- At first launch, only a limited set of cars, tracks, challenges, and background music is available.\n- Unlocks cost \"OutRun Miles,\" which are earned through progression. Missions don't have to be finished to earn them.\n- Some content is cut compared with the home version of *OutRun 2*: the original 1986 *OutRun* and the bonus tracks from *Daytona USA 2* and *Scud Race*.\n- On PS2 and PSP, some cars, music tracks, and course variations require cross-system connectivity or cheat codes. The Japanese PS2 version includes all PSP unlockables from the start.\n\n**Multiplayer**\n- Local and internet multiplayer are supported, with online play for up to six players.\n- The PS2 and PSP versions can link up with each other.\n- The PC, PS2, and PSP online services were discontinued in May 2009. Xbox Live servers went offline on April 15, 2010. The Xbox version remains playable online through the unofficial Insignia service.\n\n**Not covered in the article**\nThe article does not describe the branching route structure, stage count, detailed drift or handling model, traffic and time-extension mechanics, scoring beyond heart points, the \"Flag to Flag\" mode, the music track list or radio, playable characters, or the game's tone in detail. The only tonal hint is an *Edge* quote praising its escape from \"war-torn deserts and space marines.\"\n\n**Reception highlights**\n- Aggregate scores: GameRankings and Metacritic put the PC version at 83%/81, PS2 at 80%/81, PSP at 83%/82, and Xbox at 77%/77.\n- *Eurogamer* gave all four versions 9/10.\n- *Edge* gave the PSP version 8/10 and ranked the game #71 in its 2014 \"The 100 Best Games to Play Today.\" In 2017, it was one of only two racing games on the magazine's all-time top 100 list."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"f0c079db-350c-4d7a-848c-0bf55d95458f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:29.014Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":199917,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast: Gameplay Summary\n\n**Core driving and cars**\n- Gameplay is similar to earlier *OutRun 2* versions. Cars are grouped into classes from Novice to Professional. Higher classes have greater top speeds and weaker handling.\n- A separate \"OutRun\" class gives each car better performance in all areas, plus cosmetic changes such as racing stripes, decals, and reworked bodywork.\n- The game has 15 cars, the most of any *OutRun* title. Ten come from *OutRun 2 SP*, and new models include the 550 Barchetta, F355 Spider, Superamerica, 328 GTS, and F430.\n\n**Modes**\n- **Coast 2 Coast** is the career mode. Its missions include racing rivals for first place, fulfilling a passenger's requests for specific driving maneuvers, and tests of memory and logic.\n- Returning from *OutRun 2 SP* are the \"OutRun,\" \"Heart Attack,\" and \"Time Attack\" modes.\n- Four modes are exclusive to Coast 2 Coast:\n  - **Test Your Drift:** A one-on-one race where points come from drifting through bends.\n  - **Test Your Slipstream:** Drive behind traffic to collect points and beat rivals.\n  - **Avoid the Knockout:** The last-placed car at the end of each stage is eliminated.\n  - **Don't Lose Your Girlfriend:** A one-on-one duel to stay ahead of a rival couple until their \"heart points\" reach 0.\n\n**Unlocks**\n- At first launch, only a limited set of cars, tracks, challenges, and background music is available.\n- Unlocks cost \"OutRun Miles,\" which are earned through progression. Missions don't have to be finished to earn them.\n- Some content is cut compared with the home version of *OutRun 2*: the original 1986 *OutRun* and the bonus tracks from *Daytona USA 2* and *Scud Race*.\n- On PS2 and PSP, some cars, music tracks, and course variations require cross-system connectivity or cheat codes. The Japanese PS2 version includes all PSP unlockables from the start.\n\n**Multiplayer**\n- Local and internet multiplayer are supported, with online play for up to six players.\n- The PS2 and PSP versions can link up with each other.\n- The PC, PS2, and PSP online services were discontinued in May 2009. Xbox Live servers went offline on April 15, 2010. The Xbox version remains playable online through the unofficial Insignia service.\n\n**Not covered in the article**\nThe article does not describe the branching route structure, stage count, detailed drift or handling model, traffic and time-extension mechanics, scoring beyond heart points, the \"Flag to Flag\" mode, the music track list or radio, playable characters, or the game's tone in detail. The only tonal hint is an *Edge* quote praising its escape from \"war-torn deserts and space marines.\"\n\n**Reception highlights**\n- Aggregate scores: GameRankings and Metacritic put the PC version at 83%/81, PS2 at 80%/81, PSP at 83%/82, and Xbox at 77%/77.\n- *Eurogamer* gave all four versions 9/10.\n- *Edge* gave the PSP version 8/10 and ranked the game #71 in its 2014 \"The 100 Best Games to Play Today.\" In 2017, it was one of only two racing games on the magazine's all-time top 100 list.","durationMs":12349,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OutRun_2006:_Coast_2_Coast"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PWpEC59CP7WVmjuCQLPQdc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
