{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EBNeGs6DJRjJF5qX9fQjYs","type":"tool_result","content":"The article is a retrospective, not a manual, so it covers many of the requested topics only briefly or not at all.\n\n**Driving and drifting**\n- Handling is deliberately unrealistic. You stay on the road ahead and mostly shift your horizontal position rather than \"turning\" in the usual sense.\n- Drifting around corners keeps your speed up. It's initiated with a simple tap of the brakes.\n- Slipstreaming other traffic or rival racers helps, especially on harder challenges.\n\n**Traffic and rivals:** Traffic and rival racers matter mainly as slipstream opportunities and as obstacles in Heart Attack requests. No further detail is given.\n\n**Time extensions, route branching, stage count, goals/endings, OutRun miles, music/radio, HUD details:** Not covered in the article. The only presentation notes are giant on-screen numbers that give immediate feedback on performance, plus bright blue skies and colourful visuals.\n\n**Heart Attack mode**\n- You race against the clock while completing escalating requests from your girlfriend, such as smashing cars out of the way, drifting around corners, and breaking \"tapes\" between pairs of cars.\n- Good performance earns Heart Points, which represent how much she likes you.\n- At the end of the race you receive a grade based on overall performance. Rank letters, heart ratings, and scoring details are not specified.\n\n**Coast 2 Coast career mode**\n- Missions are assigned by characters, not laid out on a grid map. No licences or ranks are mentioned.\n- Flagman's missions focus on racing: winning races or drifting as much as possible.\n- The three girlfriend characters' missions are mostly based on Heart Attack, with some added twists.\n- Missions are shorter and usually cover one or two stages from the arcade course.\n- Some girlfriend missions require driving the full course to unlock the sub-missions needed for her full approval.\n- The package also includes the full OutRun 2 SP arcade game.\n\n**Characters and tone**\n- The protagonist is a mid-life-crisis driver with a new Ferrari and a girlfriend who is likely after his money.\n- The article doesn't name the girlfriends or give their personalities, and it doesn't quote any of their dialogue.\n- The writing is wry and playful. Lines such as \"Every man's worst nightmare.\" set a humorous, self-aware tone for the Heart Attack mode."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"0fd75619-a37a-40ed-bd2c-516b1a03f3d2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:51:44.811Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":245884,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The article is a retrospective, not a manual, so it covers many of the requested topics only briefly or not at all.\n\n**Driving and drifting**\n- Handling is deliberately unrealistic. You stay on the road ahead and mostly shift your horizontal position rather than \"turning\" in the usual sense.\n- Drifting around corners keeps your speed up. It's initiated with a simple tap of the brakes.\n- Slipstreaming other traffic or rival racers helps, especially on harder challenges.\n\n**Traffic and rivals:** Traffic and rival racers matter mainly as slipstream opportunities and as obstacles in Heart Attack requests. No further detail is given.\n\n**Time extensions, route branching, stage count, goals/endings, OutRun miles, music/radio, HUD details:** Not covered in the article. The only presentation notes are giant on-screen numbers that give immediate feedback on performance, plus bright blue skies and colourful visuals.\n\n**Heart Attack mode**\n- You race against the clock while completing escalating requests from your girlfriend, such as smashing cars out of the way, drifting around corners, and breaking \"tapes\" between pairs of cars.\n- Good performance earns Heart Points, which represent how much she likes you.\n- At the end of the race you receive a grade based on overall performance. Rank letters, heart ratings, and scoring details are not specified.\n\n**Coast 2 Coast career mode**\n- Missions are assigned by characters, not laid out on a grid map. No licences or ranks are mentioned.\n- Flagman's missions focus on racing: winning races or drifting as much as possible.\n- The three girlfriend characters' missions are mostly based on Heart Attack, with some added twists.\n- Missions are shorter and usually cover one or two stages from the arcade course.\n- Some girlfriend missions require driving the full course to unlock the sub-missions needed for her full approval.\n- The package also includes the full OutRun 2 SP arcade game.\n\n**Characters and tone**\n- The protagonist is a mid-life-crisis driver with a new Ferrari and a girlfriend who is likely after his money.\n- The article doesn't name the girlfriends or give their personalities, and it doesn't quote any of their dialogue.\n- The writing is wry and playful. Lines such as \"Every man's worst nightmare.\" set a humorous, self-aware tone for the Heart Attack mode.","durationMs":9859,"url":"https://moegamer.net/2017/08/01/outrun-2006-gone-but-not-forgotten/"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EBNeGs6DJRjJF5qX9fQjYs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
