{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyZP4iF9mzjnG7JVu7W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0167yFVYaxsiTooTcd756ukr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/opus-plan-x531263/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n -i \"slider\\|range\\b\\|min:\\|symbols\\|glyph\\|lastDevice\\|label(\" API-INDEX.md | head -40","description":"Search the API index for sliders and input glyphs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":150422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1460},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"a4017eac-2466-4f5a-81d4-88076753c9c9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:00.979Z","request_id":"req_011CggyZNqK2SGtAJCFZXjhY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0167yFVYaxsiTooTcd756ukr":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/opus-plan-x531263/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n -i \"slider\\|range\\b\\|min:\\|symbols\\|glyph\\|lastDevice\\|label(\" API-INDEX.md | head -40","description":"Search the API index for sliders and input glyphs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0167yFVYaxsiTooTcd756ukr","type":"tool_result","content":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n116:- `E.versionLabel()`: 'v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': the label to show on screens and in reports\n166:- `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)`: melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional) also limits the height difference, so a hero on a roof can't hit a guard in the street (left out, height is ignored)\n187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle around facing, radians; default all round), facing (default from.facing), dz (most height difference, default E.HEIGHTS.level), sight: map (only those its eyes see), filter: t => bool }. A target's r adds to the range\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n505:- `game.start({ camera })`: a scene's { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5, wheel: true }: the player zooms the camera within zoom (the wheel, - and =, a pinch, Settings, Camera zoom: theirs, kept, on top of the game's; false or none: they can't; a function of the game: a range per screen shape, g => [g.upright ? 1 : .85, 2]), from start, the zoom it starts at (tall: on a screen held upright, game.upright; 1 without); wheel: false leaves the mouse wheel to the game\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, on top of the game's zoom), and noted at the top of the screen ('ZOOM 1.65x': the number a scene's camera.start takes). Does nothing where the scene doesn't let the player zoom. Returns the zoom\n512:- `game.zoomRange()` †: the zooms the player may take the camera to here, [min, max] (the scene's camera.zoom, or the game's; a function of the game gives one per screen shape or level), or null where they can't (camera.zoom false or none)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n758:- `map.landing(from, dir, o = {})`: where a jump from `from` in direction dir lands across a gap: past the first drop ahead (a top more than step below its feet), the nearest spot min..max away that rises at most rise and falls at most drop from its feet, stands above the gap's bottom, has room to stand, and that a jump arc peaking apex above the higher end clears (arcClear). { x, y, z, d } or null (a wall before any gap, or nowhere to land). o: { min: 35, max: 83, rise: 11, drop: 18, apex: 20 }\n759:- `map.ledge(from, dir, o = {})`: a ledge to climb: in direction dir from `from`, the nearest top that rises min..rise above its feet within reach, with room to stand past the edge, looking straight ahead and spread radians to each side (a gap first means a jump: landing). { x, y, z (the spot to stand on top), rise, facing (the angle climbed), edge: [x, y] (where the hands grip) } or null. o: { reach: 18, min: 4, rise: 82, spread: .28 }\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1311:- `car.charge = 0`: a kart's drift boost building (1 blue, 2 orange)\n1364:- `new E.Fighter(game, o = {}) → fighter` †: new E.Fighter(game, { name, x, side: 1 (faces right), rig: Humanoid options (or a Humanoid), life: 1000, walk: 75, back: 60, jump: 390, jumpX: 90, moves, throwBtn: 'hp', throwRange, throwDmg: 120, input })\n1427:- `E.gen.rooms(w, h, o = {})`: rooms placed apart and joined in order by bent corridors: { rows, rooms, start, end, marks }. o: { seed, rooms: 9, min: 4, max: 9 (a room's side, cells) }\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [units] }: a threat map, for an AI's safe cells and a player's warning tint\n1487:- `E.tint(r, cells, color, alpha = .4, T = 16, height = null)`: tints on cells' tops: E.tint(r, cells ([[cx, cy], ...]), color, alpha = .4, T = 16, height(cx, cy) = 0): a move range, a path, an attack's reach, drawn on the floor (decals) where height is 0; on a raised top (a TileMap wall's) it sorts with the map: over that top, under whoever stands on it, behind what is in front\n1679:- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174755__x531263/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"93a12a27-8b7f-4640-aeff-6d5b2e7b9236",