{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HCzDb4GDhFQui9LcSsRD4","type":"tool_result","content":"1220\t## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1221\t\n1222\t- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1223\t- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n1224\t- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1225\t- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n1226\t- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n1227\t- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n1228\t- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n1229\t- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n1230\t- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n1231\t- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n1232\t- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n1233\t- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234\t- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1235\t- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n1236\t- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n1237\t- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n1238\t- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1239\t- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n1240\t- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n1241\t- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1242\t- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n1243\t- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n1244\t- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n1245\t- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n1246\t- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n1247\t- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n1248\t- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n1249\t- `arcade.o`: the options\n1250\t- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n1251\t- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n1252\t- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n1253\t- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\n1254\t\n1255\t## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"7f90a3ec-f29d-462a-8945-58a8f9b1b648","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:11.179Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/opus-plan-x531263/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","content":"## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n- `arcade.o`: the options\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\n\n## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)","numLines":36,"startLine":1220,"totalLines":1745}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011HCzDb4GDhFQui9LcSsRD4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
