{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012zCrgbEN6hvoRQ8cgFWNKy","type":"tool_result","content":"1573\t## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1574\t\n1575\t- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n1576\t- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\n1577\t- `road.ahead(h = this.o.height)`: how far past the camera the player's car stands when drawn at the screen's bottom, for a camera h over the road\n1578\t- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\n1579\t- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\n1580\t- `road.hits(z, x, w)`: the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches\n1581\t- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }\n1582\t- `road.project(z, x, y = 0)`: a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn, or null behind it\n1583\t- `road.seg(z)`: the segment at a distance (it wraps)\n1584\t- `road.yAt(z)`: the road's height at a distance\n1585\t- `road.depth`: the camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width)\n1586\t- `road.length = 0`: the lap in world units\n1587\t- `road.o`: its options (colors over the defaults)\n1588\t- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\n1589\t\n1590\t## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"e9cdb801-deb1-4ec9-9983-34b480d6a16d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:13.605Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/opus-plan-x531263/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","content":"## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n\n- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\n- `road.ahead(h = this.o.height)`: how far past the camera the player's car stands when drawn at the screen's bottom, for a camera h over the road\n- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\n- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\n- `road.hits(z, x, w)`: the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches\n- `road.place(z, offset, what, scale = 8)`: scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w }\n- `road.project(z, x, y = 0)`: a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn, or null behind it\n- `road.seg(z)`: the segment at a distance (it wraps)\n- `road.yAt(z)`: the road's height at a distance\n- `road.depth`: the camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width)\n- `road.length = 0`: the lap in world units\n- `road.o`: its options (colors over the defaults)\n- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\n\n## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)","numLines":18,"startLine":1573,"totalLines":1745}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012zCrgbEN6hvoRQ8cgFWNKy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
