{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XWKDHWu8L1JGW3fnegTKC1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast\n2\t\n3\t> *One day. One road. Every flower in bloom.*\n4\t\n5\tThis is the build plan for a feature-complete demo inspired by **OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast**. Read it together with\n6\t`TASK.md`; where the two seem to disagree, `TASK.md` wins and this plan bends.\n7\t\n8\t**Title.** It was picked the way `TASK.md` asks: fifty playful riffs on the source's name were brainstormed silently,\n9\tthen Python's `secrets.randbelow(50)` drew #49, **OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast**. The title is final, so don't re-roll it.\n10\t\"Bloom\" carries three meanings and the whole design leans on them: flowers (the world), love in bloom (the passenger),\n11\tand the over-bright 2000s *bloom lighting* the source era is remembered for (the look).\n12\t\n13\t**The pitch.** An arcade road racer on the engine's pixel-art pseudo-3D road. You drive an open-top dream car, with a\n14\tdemanding passenger beside you, across the island of **Bellafiore** in a single day. You start on the Alba Coast at\n15\tsunrise and race to the Vespera Coast before the sun sets. A run is five one-minute stages. At every checkpoint the road\n16\tforks, so you choose your own route: 15 stages, 16 routes and 5 goals, each goal with its own ending. A clock counts down\n17\tthe whole way, and traffic, drifts, slipstreams and your passenger's whims fill the minutes in between.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## Contents\n22\t\n23\t1. Quick facts\n24\t2. What makes the source distinctive, and how OutBloom plays it\n25\t3. Originality rules\n26\t4. Deliverables, folders and setup\n27\t5. Architecture\n28\t6. Engine changes\n29\t7. Systems (the full spec of every mechanic)\n30\t8. Content (world, stages, goals, cars, cast, traffic, requests, missions, unlocks, music, writing)\n31\t9. Art direction and asset recipes\n32\t10. Build order and milestones\n33\t11. Risks and how to de-risk them\n34\t12. Testing\n35\t13. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement and where it lives\n36\t- Appendices: A. tuning defaults (the dev sliders) · B. input map · C. glyphs · D. the debug handle and events · E. research notes\n37\t\n38\t---\n39\t\n40\t## 1. Quick facts\n41\t\n42\t| | |\n43\t|---|---|\n44\t| Genre | Arcade road racing: an OutRun-style checkpoint racer. A passenger-request \"date\" layer (*Love in Bloom*) and a mission career (*Coast 2 Coast Tour*) sit on top. |\n45\t| Perspective | Third-person chase camera behind the car, on a sprite-scaled pseudo-3D road (the engine's `road` module). Also a high chase and a bumper camera. Side-view vignettes for the start line, endings and the garage, and a stylised overhead map for the career. |\n46\t| Players | 1 in every mode. 2 on one machine, split screen (*Versus*). 1–4 online in AI Hub *ghost* sessions. |\n47\t| Engine | my-3D2dge **v0.85.2** handoff package (`dist/handoff`, commit `4390a98`), the full engine with every module, changed as listed in §6. |\n48\t| Look | Engine-native pixel art at 480×270 (`expand: true`), with a pixel-safe bloom pass, lens flare and dithered fog. |\n49\t| Audio | Everything is synthesised in code with the engine's chip synth, extended with instruments and effects (§6, §7.14–7.16). Voices are syllable-synth gibberish. |\n50\t| Deliverable | One self-contained HTML file in this folder's root, plus `exit-interview.json` beside it. |\n51\t\n52\t**Names.** Take the model/effort/timestamp part from *your* `TASK.md`. With this `TASK.md` the names are:\n53\t\n54\t- GameTitle slug: `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast`. SOURCE slug: `OutRun2006Coast2Coast` (spaces and punctuation removed, words joined).\n55\t- Dev folder: `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174755/`\n56\t- Bundle: `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174755.html`, in the root, beside `TASK.md`.\n57\t- Exit interview: `exit-interview.json`, in the root.\n58\t- The title on screen and in `aiHub.name` reads exactly **OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast**.\n59\t\n60\t---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13","uuid":"2a730969-fc4f-4183-8d29-e06a95761027","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:05.055Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174755__x531263/work/PLAN.md","content":"# OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast\n\n> *One day. One road. Every flower in bloom.*\n\nThis is the build plan for a feature-complete demo inspired by **OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast**. Read it together with\n`TASK.md`; where the two seem to disagree, `TASK.md` wins and this plan bends.\n\n**Title.** It was picked the way `TASK.md` asks: fifty playful riffs on the source's name were brainstormed silently,\nthen Python's `secrets.randbelow(50)` drew #49, **OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast**. The title is final, so don't re-roll it.\n\"Bloom\" carries three meanings and the whole design leans on them: flowers (the world), love in bloom (the passenger),\nand the over-bright 2000s *bloom lighting* the source era is remembered for (the look).\n\n**The pitch.** An arcade road racer on the engine's pixel-art pseudo-3D road. You drive an open-top dream car, with a\ndemanding passenger beside you, across the island of **Bellafiore** in a single day. You start on the Alba Coast at\nsunrise and race to the Vespera Coast before the sun sets. A run is five one-minute stages. At every checkpoint the road\nforks, so you choose your own route: 15 stages, 16 routes and 5 goals, each goal with its own ending. A clock counts down\nthe whole way, and traffic, drifts, slipstreams and your passenger's whims fill the minutes in between.\n\n---\n\n## Contents\n\n1. Quick facts\n2. What makes the source distinctive, and how OutBloom plays it\n3. Originality rules\n4. Deliverables, folders and setup\n5. Architecture\n6. Engine changes\n7. Systems (the full spec of every mechanic)\n8. Content (world, stages, goals, cars, cast, traffic, requests, missions, unlocks, music, writing)\n9. Art direction and asset recipes\n10. Build order and milestones\n11. Risks and how to de-risk them\n12. Testing\n13. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement and where it lives\n- Appendices: A. tuning defaults (the dev sliders) · B. input map · C. glyphs · D. the debug handle and events · E. research notes\n\n---\n\n## 1. Quick facts\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Genre | Arcade road racing: an OutRun-style checkpoint racer. A passenger-request \"date\" layer (*Love in Bloom*) and a mission career (*Coast 2 Coast Tour*) sit on top. |\n| Perspective | Third-person chase camera behind the car, on a sprite-scaled pseudo-3D road (the engine's `road` module). Also a high chase and a bumper camera. Side-view vignettes for the start line, endings and the garage, and a stylised overhead map for the career. |\n| Players | 1 in every mode. 2 on one machine, split screen (*Versus*). 1–4 online in AI Hub *ghost* sessions. |\n| Engine | my-3D2dge **v0.85.2** handoff package (`dist/handoff`, commit `4390a98`), the full engine with every module, changed as listed in §6. |\n| Look | Engine-native pixel art at 480×270 (`expand: true`), with a pixel-safe bloom pass, lens flare and dithered fog. |\n| Audio | Everything is synthesised in code with the engine's chip synth, extended with instruments and effects (§6, §7.14–7.16). Voices are syllable-synth gibberish. |\n| Deliverable | One self-contained HTML file in this folder's root, plus `exit-interview.json` beside it. |\n\n**Names.** Take the model/effort/timestamp part from *your* `TASK.md`. With this `TASK.md` the names are:\n\n- GameTitle slug: `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast`. SOURCE slug: `OutRun2006Coast2Coast` (spaces and punctuation removed, words joined).\n- Dev folder: `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174755/`\n- Bundle: `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174755.html`, in the root, beside `TASK.md`.\n- Exit interview: `exit-interview.json`, in the root.\n- The title on screen and in `aiHub.name` reads exactly **OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast**.\n\n---","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1758}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XWKDHWu8L1JGW3fnegTKC1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
